Use XMX and XMS
When you build java applications then it creates a .jar file, then you run the application by using java -jar command followed by the jar file that has been created.

XMX is an argument which you pass in the command
For e.g java -Xmx5Gi -jar test.jar

Xmx specifies the max mem allocation and xms specifies initial mem allocation to start a Java application


